    "question": {
      "pdfName": "Theory_of_Computation_2.pdf",
      "direction": "Directions for questions 1 to 25: Select the correct alternative from the given choices.",
      "text": "Consider the regular expression, RE = $ab^* + ba^*$. Then the reversal of RE, given by $RE^R$ is equal to:",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$ab^* + ba^*$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$a^*b$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$b^*a + a^*b$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$(a^*b)(b^*a)$"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$b^*a + a^*b$",
      "explanation": "Given regular expression, $RE = ab^* + ba^*$. $RE^R = (ab^* + ba^*)^R = (ab^*)^R + (ba^*)^R = (b^*)^R a^R + (a^*)^R b^R = (b^R)^*a + (a^R)^*b = b^*a + a^*b$ Choice (C)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Theory of Computation",
      "topic": "Regular expressions",
      "subtopic": null,
      "tags": []
    },
